Edge match (0019) with Far depth (0015): the scale k (one periphery texel in focus texels) comes from the derivatives
of the focus coordinate as the view projects it, never from the one Far depth displaced. The displacement jumps across
a depth edge, and its derivative read as a huge k there: a halo of blur, patchy along depth edges inside the fade band.
The same text in ProjectionPS.hlsl and in the copy Far depth keeps (ProjectionPS.nofardepth.hlsl), after the anchors
Far depth's injection uses. With dcsvr_edge_match 0 the sizes and derivatives are no longer computed at all (one
branch on the constant for the draw); the composition is unchanged (tests/quadviews-composition).

